<div id=3D"installation">
  <div class=3D"os macos">
<h1 class=3D"no_toc" id=3D"installing-on-macos">Installing on macOS</h1>

<p>PyTorch can be installed and used on macOS. Depending on your system and=
 GPU capabilities, your experience with PyTorch on a Mac may vary in terms =
of processing time.</p>

<h2 id=3D"mac-prerequisites">Prerequisites<a class=3D"anchorjs-link " href=
=3D"https://pytorch.org/get-started/locally/#mac-prerequisites" aria-label=
=3D"Anchor" data-anchorjs-icon=3D"=EE=A7=8B" style=3D"font: 1em / 1 anchorj=
s-icons; padding-left: 0.375em;"></a></h2>

<h3 id=3D"macos-version">macOS Version<a class=3D"anchorjs-link " href=3D"h=
ttps://pytorch.org/get-started/locally/#macos-version" aria-label=3D"Anchor=
" data-anchorjs-icon=3D"=EE=A7=8B" style=3D"font: 1em / 1 anchorjs-icons; p=
adding-left: 0.375em;"></a></h3>

<p>PyTorch is supported on macOS 10.15 (Catalina) or above.</p>

<h3 id=3D"mac-python">Python<a class=3D"anchorjs-link " href=3D"https://pyt=
orch.org/get-started/locally/#mac-python" aria-label=3D"Anchor" data-anchor=
js-icon=3D"=EE=A7=8B" style=3D"font: 1em / 1 anchorjs-icons; padding-left: =
0.375em;"></a></h3>

<p>It is recommended that you use Python 3.8 - 3.11.
You can install Python either through the Anaconda
package manager (see <a href=3D"https://pytorch.org/get-started/locally/#an=
aconda">below</a>), <a href=3D"https://brew.sh/" target=3D"_blank">Homebrew=
</a>, or
the <a href=3D"https://www.python.org/downloads/mac-osx/" target=3D"_blank"=
>Python website</a>.</p>

<p>In one of the upcoming PyTorch releases, support for Python 3.8 will be =
deprecated.</p>

<h3 id=3D"mac-package-manager">Package Manager<a class=3D"anchorjs-link " h=
ref=3D"https://pytorch.org/get-started/locally/#mac-package-manager" aria-l=
abel=3D"Anchor" data-anchorjs-icon=3D"=EE=A7=8B" style=3D"font: 1em / 1 anc=
horjs-icons; padding-left: 0.375em;"></a></h3>

<p>To install the PyTorch binaries, you will need to use one of two support=
ed package managers: <a href=3D"https://www.anaconda.com/download/#macos" t=
arget=3D"_blank">Anaconda</a> or <a href=3D"https://pypi.org/project/pip/" =
target=3D"_blank">pip</a>. Anaconda is the recommended package manager as i=
t will provide you all of the PyTorch dependencies in one, sandboxed instal=
l, including Python.</p>

<h4 id=3D"anaconda">Anaconda<a class=3D"anchorjs-link " href=3D"https://pyt=
orch.org/get-started/locally/#anaconda" aria-label=3D"Anchor" data-anchorjs=
-icon=3D"=EE=A7=8B" style=3D"font: 1em / 1 anchorjs-icons; padding-left: 0.=
375em;"></a></h4>

<p>To install Anaconda, you can <a href=3D"https://www.anaconda.com/downloa=
d/#macos" target=3D"_blank">download graphical installer</a> or use the com=
mand-line installer. If you use the command-line installer, you can right-c=
lick on the installer link, select <code class=3D"language-plaintext highli=
ghter-rouge">Copy Link Address</code>, or use the following commands on Int=
el Mac:</p>

<div class=3D"language-bash highlighter-rouge"><div class=3D"highlight"><pr=
e class=3D"highlight"><code><span class=3D"c"># The version of Anaconda may=
 be different depending on when you are installing`</span>
curl <span class=3D"nt">-O</span> https://repo.anaconda.com/miniconda/Minic=
onda3-latest-MacOSX-x86_64.sh
sh Miniconda3-latest-MacOSX-x86_64.sh
<span class=3D"c"># and follow the prompts. The defaults are generally good=
.`</span>
</code></pre></div></div>
<p>or following commands on M1 Mac:</p>
<div class=3D"language-bash highlighter-rouge"><div class=3D"highlight"><pr=
e class=3D"highlight"><code><span class=3D"c"># The version of Anaconda may=
 be different depending on when you are installing`</span>
curl <span class=3D"nt">-O</span> https://repo.anaconda.com/miniconda/Minic=
onda3-latest-MacOSX-arm64.sh
sh Miniconda3-latest-MacOSX-arm64.sh
<span class=3D"c"># and follow the prompts. The defaults are generally good=
.`</span>
</code></pre></div></div>
<h4 id=3D"pip">pip<a class=3D"anchorjs-link " href=3D"https://pytorch.org/g=
et-started/locally/#pip" aria-label=3D"Anchor" data-anchorjs-icon=3D"=EE=A7=
=8B" style=3D"font: 1em / 1 anchorjs-icons; padding-left: 0.375em;"></a></h=
4>

<p><em>Python 3</em></p>

<p>If you installed Python via Homebrew or the Python website, <code class=
=3D"language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">pip</code> was installed with it.=
 If you installed Python 3.x, then you will be using the command <code clas=
s=3D"language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">pip3</code>.</p>

<blockquote>
  <p>Tip: If you want to use just the command  <code class=3D"language-plai=
ntext highlighter-rouge">pip</code>, instead of <code class=3D"language-pla=
intext highlighter-rouge">pip3</code>, you can symlink <code class=3D"langu=
age-plaintext highlighter-rouge">pip</code> to the <code class=3D"language-=
plaintext highlighter-rouge">pip3</code> binary.</p>
</blockquote>

<h2 id=3D"mac-installation">Installation<a class=3D"anchorjs-link " href=3D=
"https://pytorch.org/get-started/locally/#mac-installation" aria-label=3D"A=
nchor" data-anchorjs-icon=3D"=EE=A7=8B" style=3D"font: 1em / 1 anchorjs-ico=
ns; padding-left: 0.375em;"></a></h2>

<h3 id=3D"mac-anaconda">Anaconda<a class=3D"anchorjs-link " href=3D"https:/=
/pytorch.org/get-started/locally/#mac-anaconda" aria-label=3D"Anchor" data-=
anchorjs-icon=3D"=EE=A7=8B" style=3D"font: 1em / 1 anchorjs-icons; padding-=
left: 0.375em;"></a></h3>

<p>To install PyTorch via Anaconda, use the following conda command:</p>

<div class=3D"language-bash highlighter-rouge"><div class=3D"highlight"><pr=
e class=3D"highlight"><code>conda <span class=3D"nb">install </span>pytorch=
 torchvision <span class=3D"nt">-c</span> pytorch
</code></pre></div></div>

<h3 id=3D"mac-anaconda">pip<a class=3D"anchorjs-link " href=3D"https://pyto=
rch.org/get-started/locally/#mac-anaconda" aria-label=3D"Anchor" data-ancho=
rjs-icon=3D"=EE=A7=8B" style=3D"font: 1em / 1 anchorjs-icons; padding-left:=
 0.375em;"></a></h3>

<p>To install PyTorch via pip, use one of the following two commands, depen=
ding on your Python version:</p>

<div class=3D"language-bash highlighter-rouge"><div class=3D"highlight"><pr=
e class=3D"highlight"><code><span class=3D"c"># Python 3.x</span>
pip3 <span class=3D"nb">install </span>torch torchvision
</code></pre></div></div>

<h2 id=3D"mac-verification">Verification<a class=3D"anchorjs-link " href=3D=
"https://pytorch.org/get-started/locally/#mac-verification" aria-label=3D"A=
nchor" data-anchorjs-icon=3D"=EE=A7=8B" style=3D"font: 1em / 1 anchorjs-ico=
ns; padding-left: 0.375em;"></a></h2>

<p>To ensure that PyTorch was installed correctly, we can verify the instal=
lation by running sample PyTorch code. Here we will construct a randomly in=
itialized tensor.</p>

<div class=3D"language-python highlighter-rouge"><div class=3D"highlight"><=
pre class=3D"highlight"><code><span class=3D"kn">import</span> <span class=
=3D"nn">torch</span>
<span class=3D"n">x</span> <span class=3D"o">=3D</span> <span class=3D"n">t=
orch</span><span class=3D"p">.</span><span class=3D"n">rand</span><span cla=
ss=3D"p">(</span><span class=3D"mi">5</span><span class=3D"p">,</span> <spa=
n class=3D"mi">3</span><span class=3D"p">)</span>
<span class=3D"k">print</span><span class=3D"p">(</span><span class=3D"n">x=
</span><span class=3D"p">)</span>
</code></pre></div></div>

<p>The output should be something similar to:</p>

<div class=3D"language-plaintext highlighter-rouge"><div class=3D"highlight=
"><pre class=3D"highlight"><code>tensor([[0.3380, 0.3845, 0.3217],
        [0.8337, 0.9050, 0.2650],
        [0.2979, 0.7141, 0.9069],
        [0.1449, 0.1132, 0.1375],
        [0.4675, 0.3947, 0.1426]])
</code></pre></div></div>

<h2 id=3D"mac-from-source">Building from source<a class=3D"anchorjs-link " =
href=3D"https://pytorch.org/get-started/locally/#mac-from-source" aria-labe=
l=3D"Anchor" data-anchorjs-icon=3D"=EE=A7=8B" style=3D"font: 1em / 1 anchor=
js-icons; padding-left: 0.375em;"></a></h2>

<p>For the majority of PyTorch users, installing from a pre-built binary vi=
a a package manager will provide the best experience. However, there are ti=
mes when you may want to install the bleeding edge PyTorch code, whether fo=
r testing or actual development on the PyTorch core. To install the latest =
PyTorch code, you will need to <a href=3D"https://github.com/pytorch/pytorc=
h#from-source" target=3D"_blank">build PyTorch from source</a>.</p>

<h3 id=3D"mac-prerequisites-2">Prerequisites<a class=3D"anchorjs-link " hre=
f=3D"https://pytorch.org/get-started/locally/#mac-prerequisites-2" aria-lab=
el=3D"Anchor" data-anchorjs-icon=3D"=EE=A7=8B" style=3D"font: 1em / 1 ancho=
rjs-icons; padding-left: 0.375em;"></a></h3>

<ol>
  <li>[Optional] Install <a href=3D"https://pytorch.org/get-started/locally=
/#anaconda">Anaconda</a></li>
  <li>Follow the steps described here: <a href=3D"https://github.com/pytorc=
h/pytorch#from-source" target=3D"_blank">https://github.com/pytorch/pytorch=
#from-source</a></li>
</ol>

<p>You can verify the installation as described <a href=3D"https://pytorch.=
org/get-started/locally/#mac-verification">above</a>.</p>

</div>
  <div class=3D"os linux">
<h1 class=3D"no_toc" id=3D"installing-on-linux">Installing on Linux</h1>

<p>PyTorch can be installed and used on various Linux distributions. Depend=
ing on your system and compute requirements, your experience with PyTorch o=
n Linux may vary in terms of processing time. It is recommended, but not re=
quired, that your Linux system has an NVIDIA or AMD GPU in order to harness=
 the full power of PyTorch=E2=80=99s <a href=3D"https://developer.nvidia.co=
m/cuda-zone" target=3D"_blank">CUDA</a> <a href=3D"https://pytorch.org/tuto=
rials/beginner/blitz/tensor_tutorial.html?highlight=3Dcuda#cuda-tensors">su=
pport</a> or <a href=3D"https://docs.amd.com/" target=3D"_blank">ROCm</a> s=
upport.</p>

<h2 id=3D"linux-prerequisites">Prerequisites<a class=3D"anchorjs-link " hre=
f=3D"https://pytorch.org/get-started/locally/#linux-prerequisites" aria-lab=
el=3D"Anchor" data-anchorjs-icon=3D"=EE=A7=8B" style=3D"font: 1em / 1 ancho=
rjs-icons; padding-left: 0.375em;"></a></h2>

<h3 id=3D"supported-linux-distributions">Supported Linux Distributions<a cl=
ass=3D"anchorjs-link " href=3D"https://pytorch.org/get-started/locally/#sup=
ported-linux-distributions" aria-label=3D"Anchor" data-anchorjs-icon=3D"=EE=
=A7=8B" style=3D"font: 1em / 1 anchorjs-icons; padding-left: 0.375em;"></a>=
</h3>

<p>PyTorch is supported on Linux distributions that use <a href=3D"https://=
www.gnu.org/software/libc/" target=3D"_blank">glibc</a> &gt;=3D v2.17, whic=
h include the following:</p>

<ul>
  <li><a href=3D"https://www.archlinux.org/download/" target=3D"_blank">Arc=
h Linux</a>, minimum version 2012-07-15</li>
  <li><a href=3D"https://www.centos.org/download/" target=3D"_blank">CentOS=
</a>, minimum version 7.3-1611</li>
  <li><a href=3D"https://www.debian.org/distrib/" target=3D"_blank">Debian<=
/a>, minimum version 8.0</li>
  <li><a href=3D"https://getfedora.org/" target=3D"_blank">Fedora</a>, mini=
mum version 24</li>
  <li><a href=3D"https://linuxmint.com/download.php" target=3D"_blank">Mint=
</a>, minimum version 14</li>
  <li><a href=3D"https://software.opensuse.org/" target=3D"_blank">OpenSUSE=
</a>, minimum version 42.1</li>
  <li><a href=3D"https://www.pclinuxos.com/" target=3D"_blank">PCLinuxOS</a=
>, minimum version 2014.7</li>
  <li><a href=3D"http://www.slackware.com/getslack/" target=3D"_blank">Slac=
kware</a>, minimum version 14.2</li>
  <li><a href=3D"https://www.ubuntu.com/download/desktop" target=3D"_blank"=
>Ubuntu</a>, minimum version 13.04</li>
</ul>

<blockquote>
  <p>The install instructions here will generally apply to all supported Li=
nux distributions. An example difference is that your distribution may supp=
ort <code class=3D"language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">yum</code> instead=
 of <code class=3D"language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">apt</code>. The sp=
ecific examples shown were run on an Ubuntu 18.04 machine.</p>
</blockquote>

<h3 id=3D"linux-python">Python<a class=3D"anchorjs-link " href=3D"https://p=
