rjs-icon=3D"=EE=A7=8B" style=3D"font: 1em / 1 anchorjs-icons; padding-left:=
 0.375em;"></a></h4>

<p>To install PyTorch via Anaconda, and you do have a <a href=3D"https://de=
veloper.nvidia.com/cuda-zone" target=3D"_blank">CUDA-capable</a> system, in=
 the above selector, choose OS: Windows, Package: Conda and the CUDA versio=
n suited to your machine. Often, the latest CUDA version is better.
Then, run the command that is presented to you.</p>

<h3 id=3D"windows-pip">pip<a class=3D"anchorjs-link " href=3D"https://pytor=
ch.org/get-started/locally/#windows-pip" aria-label=3D"Anchor" data-anchorj=
s-icon=3D"=EE=A7=8B" style=3D"font: 1em / 1 anchorjs-icons; padding-left: 0=
.375em;"></a></h3>

<h4 id=3D"no-cuda-1">No CUDA<a class=3D"anchorjs-link " href=3D"https://pyt=
orch.org/get-started/locally/#no-cuda-1" aria-label=3D"Anchor" data-anchorj=
s-icon=3D"=EE=A7=8B" style=3D"font: 1em / 1 anchorjs-icons; padding-left: 0=
.375em;"></a></h4>

<p>To install PyTorch via pip, and do not have a <a href=3D"https://develop=
er.nvidia.com/cuda-zone" target=3D"_blank">CUDA-capable</a> system or do no=
t require CUDA, in the above selector, choose OS: Windows, Package: Pip and=
 CUDA: None.
Then, run the command that is presented to you.</p>

<h4 id=3D"with-cuda-1">With CUDA<a class=3D"anchorjs-link " href=3D"https:/=
/pytorch.org/get-started/locally/#with-cuda-1" aria-label=3D"Anchor" data-a=
nchorjs-icon=3D"=EE=A7=8B" style=3D"font: 1em / 1 anchorjs-icons; padding-l=
eft: 0.375em;"></a></h4>

<p>To install PyTorch via pip, and do have a <a href=3D"https://developer.n=
vidia.com/cuda-zone" target=3D"_blank">CUDA-capable</a> system, in the abov=
e selector, choose OS: Windows, Package: Pip and the CUDA version suited to=
 your machine. Often, the latest CUDA version is better.
Then, run the command that is presented to you.</p>

<h2 id=3D"windows-verification">Verification<a class=3D"anchorjs-link " hre=
f=3D"https://pytorch.org/get-started/locally/#windows-verification" aria-la=
bel=3D"Anchor" data-anchorjs-icon=3D"=EE=A7=8B" style=3D"font: 1em / 1 anch=
orjs-icons; padding-left: 0.375em;"></a></h2>

<p>To ensure that PyTorch was installed correctly, we can verify the instal=
lation by running sample PyTorch code. Here we will construct a randomly in=
itialized tensor.</p>

<p>From the command line, type:</p>

<div class=3D"language-bash highlighter-rouge"><div class=3D"highlight"><pr=
e class=3D"highlight"><code>python
</code></pre></div></div>

<p>then enter the following code:</p>

<div class=3D"language-python highlighter-rouge"><div class=3D"highlight"><=
pre class=3D"highlight"><code><span class=3D"kn">import</span> <span class=
=3D"nn">torch</span>
<span class=3D"n">x</span> <span class=3D"o">=3D</span> <span class=3D"n">t=
orch</span><span class=3D"p">.</span><span class=3D"n">rand</span><span cla=
ss=3D"p">(</span><span class=3D"mi">5</span><span class=3D"p">,</span> <spa=
n class=3D"mi">3</span><span class=3D"p">)</span>
<span class=3D"k">print</span><span class=3D"p">(</span><span class=3D"n">x=
</span><span class=3D"p">)</span>
</code></pre></div></div>

<p>The output should be something similar to:</p>

<div class=3D"language-plaintext highlighter-rouge"><div class=3D"highlight=
"><pre class=3D"highlight"><code>tensor([[0.3380, 0.3845, 0.3217],
        [0.8337, 0.9050, 0.2650],
        [0.2979, 0.7141, 0.9069],
        [0.1449, 0.1132, 0.1375],
        [0.4675, 0.3947, 0.1426]])
</code></pre></div></div>

<p>Additionally, to check if your GPU driver and CUDA is enabled and access=
ible by PyTorch, run the following commands to return whether or not the CU=
DA driver is enabled:</p>

<div class=3D"language-python highlighter-rouge"><div class=3D"highlight"><=
pre class=3D"highlight"><code><span class=3D"kn">import</span> <span class=
=3D"nn">torch</span>
<span class=3D"n">torch</span><span class=3D"p">.</span><span class=3D"n">c=
uda</span><span class=3D"p">.</span><span class=3D"n">is_available</span><s=
pan class=3D"p">()</span>
</code></pre></div></div>

<h2 id=3D"windows-from-source">Building from source<a class=3D"anchorjs-lin=
k " href=3D"https://pytorch.org/get-started/locally/#windows-from-source" a=
ria-label=3D"Anchor" data-anchorjs-icon=3D"=EE=A7=8B" style=3D"font: 1em / =
1 anchorjs-icons; padding-left: 0.375em;"></a></h2>

<p>For the majority of PyTorch users, installing from a pre-built binary vi=
a a package manager will provide the best experience. However, there are ti=
mes when you may want to install the bleeding edge PyTorch code, whether fo=
r testing or actual development on the PyTorch core. To install the latest =
PyTorch code, you will need to <a href=3D"https://github.com/pytorch/pytorc=
h#from-source" target=3D"_blank">build PyTorch from source</a>.</p>

<h3 id=3D"windows-prerequisites-2">Prerequisites<a class=3D"anchorjs-link "=
 href=3D"https://pytorch.org/get-started/locally/#windows-prerequisites-2" =
aria-label=3D"Anchor" data-anchorjs-icon=3D"=EE=A7=8B" style=3D"font: 1em /=
 1 anchorjs-icons; padding-left: 0.375em;"></a></h3>

<ol>
  <li>Install <a href=3D"https://pytorch.org/get-started/locally/#anaconda"=
>Anaconda</a></li>
  <li>Install <a href=3D"https://developer.nvidia.com/cuda-downloads" targe=
t=3D"_blank">CUDA</a>, if your machine has a <a href=3D"https://developer.n=
vidia.com/cuda-gpus" target=3D"_blank">CUDA-enabled GPU</a>.</li>
  <li>If you want to build on Windows, Visual Studio with MSVC toolset, and=
 NVTX are also needed. The exact requirements of those dependencies could b=
e found out <a href=3D"https://github.com/pytorch/pytorch#from-source" targ=
et=3D"_blank">here</a>.</li>
  <li>Follow the steps described here: <a href=3D"https://github.com/pytorc=
h/pytorch#from-source" target=3D"_blank">https://github.com/pytorch/pytorch=
#from-source</a></li>
</ol>

<p>You can verify the installation as described <a href=3D"https://pytorch.=
org/get-started/locally/#windows-verification">above</a>.</p>

</div>
